Drop `aero.css` into any page and plain HTML turns [[frutiger-aero|Frutiger Aero]]: sky gradients, =B=glossy buttons=B=, soft glass panels and bright links. The **Preview** shows it on a sample page with every common element!

~~~ file: aero.css
body {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #bfe6ff 0%, #effaff 320px, #ffffff 100%);
    color: #10324d;
    font-family: "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
}
h1, h2, h3 { color: #0a5c99; text-shadow: 0 1px 0 #fff; }
h1 { border-bottom: 3px solid #7fd3ff; padding-bottom: 4px; }
a { color: #0284c7; }
mark { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #fff7c2, #ffe066); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0 3px; }
code { background: #e0f2fe; border: 1px solid #bae6fd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 1px 5px; }

button {
    padding: 7px 18px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 60, 120, 0.45);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 40, 90, 0.5);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 50%, transparent 51%), linear-gradient(180deg, #7fd3ff, #0a74c9);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8), 0 3px 8px rgba(10, 116, 201, 0.3);
    cursor: pointer;
}
button.gel-green { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 50%, transparent 51%), linear-gradient(180deg, #b6f08a, #2e9a1c); }
button:disabled { filter: grayscale(1); opacity: 0.6; }
input, select, textarea {
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border: 1px solid #9cc9ea;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff, #f2f9ff);
}
blockquote { margin: 12px 0; padding: 10px 16px; border-left: 5px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 10px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); }
table { border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0; border: 1px solid #9cc9ea; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
th { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #7fd3ff, #2b8fdc); color: #fff; }
th, td { padding: 6px 14px; }
tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #eef8ff; }
.card { margin-top: 14px; padding: 4px 16px 10px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6); box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 60, 120, 0.15); }
~~~

The classic [[frutiger-aero|Frutiger Aero]] =B=gel button=B=, made with two files and no pictures! The shine is a second gradient on top, and the glow is a box shadow.

Open `gel-button.html` in a browser to see it, or copy the CSS into your own page!

~~~ file: gel-button.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Gel button</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="gel-button.css">
</head>
<body>
    <button class="gel">Click me!</button>
    <button class="gel gel-green">Go!</button>
</body>
</html>
~~~

~~~ file: gel-button.css
body {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 60px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #bfe6ff, #effaff);
    font-family: "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
}

/* the gel: a bright top half, a deeper bottom half, and a white shine */
.gel {
    --a: #7fd3ff;
    --b: #0a74c9;
    position: relative;
    padding: 12px 30px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 60, 120, 0.45);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 40, 90, 0.5);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--a) 0%, var(--b) 100%);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8), 0 4px 12px rgba(10, 116, 201, 0.35);
    cursor: pointer;
    overflow: hidden;
}
.gel::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 6%;
    right: 6%;
    top: 2px;
    height: 48%;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1));
    pointer-events: none;
}
.gel:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
.gel:active { box-shadow: inset 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 40, 90, 0.45), 0 0 18px rgba(127, 211, 255, 0.9); }
.gel:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #ffb347; outline-offset: 3px; }
.gel-green { --a: #b6f08a; --b: #2e9a1c; }
~~~

A **Poolside** water surface as a #C#Godot 4# spatial shader! Put it on a plane (a `PlaneMesh` in Godot, or **Add, Plane** in [Zonerider](https://radii-office.com/zonerider/)) and it shimmers by itself.

* `deep` and `shallow` are the two blues of the water
* `glint` is the warm orange of sunlight on the ripples
* `speed` and `scale` change how fast and how big the caustics are

In Zonerider, select the plane and, in its **Godot shader** section, choose **Open .gdshader…** and pick `poolside_water.gdshader`! Fork this lite to make your own colors!

~~~ file: poolside_water.gdshader
shader_type spatial;
render_mode specular_schlick_ggx;

uniform vec4 deep : source_color = vec4(0.02, 0.36, 0.72, 1.0);
uniform vec4 shallow : source_color = vec4(0.13, 0.83, 0.93, 1.0);
uniform vec4 glint : source_color = vec4(0.98, 0.57, 0.24, 1.0);
uniform float speed : hint_range(0.0, 3.0) = 0.6;
uniform float scale : hint_range(1.0, 20.0) = 6.0;

// soft cells that drift: the bright lines between them look like pool caustics
float caustic(vec2 p, float t) {
	vec2 i = floor(p);
	vec2 f = fract(p);
	float best = 1.0;
	for (int y = -1; y <= 1; y++) {
		for (int x = -1; x <= 1; x++) {
			vec2 g = vec2(float(x), float(y));
			vec2 o = fract(sin(vec2(dot(i + g, vec2(127.1, 311.7)), dot(i + g, vec2(269.5, 183.3)))) * 43758.5453);
			o = 0.5 + 0.5 * sin(t + 6.2831 * o);
			best = min(best, length(g + o - f));
		}
	}
	return best;
}

void fragment() {
	float t = TIME * speed;
	float c = caustic(UV * scale, t);
	float lines = pow(1.0 - c, 6.0);
	vec3 water = mix(deep.rgb, shallow.rgb, smoothstep(0.0, 0.9, UV.y + 0.15 * sin(t + UV.x * 4.0)));
	ALBEDO = water + lines * 0.55;
	EMISSION = glint.rgb * smoothstep(0.82, 1.0, lines) * 0.9;
	ROUGHNESS = 0.08;
	METALLIC = 0.0;
	SPECULAR = 0.7;
}
~~~

~~~ file: README.kd
# Poolside water

A Godot 4 spatial shader, public domain (CC0)!

* Godot: make a ShaderMaterial, load poolside_water.gdshader, and set it on a PlaneMesh
* Zonerider: select the plane, then Godot shader, Open .gdshader
* Colors: cyan and blue water, orange glints
